00:15:19.492 --> 00:15:22.730
Long term memory retrieval. Volume 47.


00:15:22.755 --> 00:15:25.228
- No.
- Woo. A real page turner.


00:15:25.253 --> 00:15:29.247
Long term memory data
selection via channel sober be.


00:15:29.272 --> 00:15:31.550
See. Fun already. Oh, you lucky dog.


00:15:31.575 --> 00:15:36.495
You're reading these cool things,
I got to go work. Life is so unfair.


00:15:42.071 --> 00:15:44.031
Ugh.


00:15:44.466 --> 00:15:48.288
What can we do. We only got capital
that'll last a month maybe two.


00:15:48.313 --> 00:15:51.750
If we can't find investors by then,
we're gonna have to lay people off.


00:15:51.775 --> 00:15:55.000
Mom. Dad. Come kiss me good night.


00:15:55.025 --> 00:15:59.072
- I know. I know. We got to land this, okay.
- Be right there.


00:16:01.796 --> 00:16:05.259
Did you hear Dad? He
sounded really upset.


00:16:07.505 --> 00:16:09.405
What was that? Was it
a bear? It's a bear!


00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:11.065
There are no bears in San Francisco.


00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:13.189
I saw a really hairy guy.
He looked like a bear.


00:16:13.214 --> 00:16:15.393
Oh. I'm so jumpy, my nerves are shocked.


00:16:15.418 --> 00:16:17.070
Ew. I don't wanna
hear about your nerves.


00:16:17.095 --> 00:16:19.767
I'll tell you what it is.
This move has been a bust.


00:16:19.792 --> 00:16:21.389
That's what I've been telling you guys.


00:16:21.414 --> 00:16:23.768
There're at least 37 things for
Riley to be scared of right now.


00:16:23.793 --> 00:16:25.435
This smell alone is
enough to make her gag.


00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:27.413
I can't believe Mom
and Dad moved us here.


00:16:27.438 --> 00:16:29.866
Look. I get it. You guys have concerns.


00:16:29.891 --> 00:16:31.326
But we've been through worst.


00:16:31.352 --> 00:16:35.345
Tell you what. Let's make a list of all
the things Riley should be happy about.


00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:37.956
Fine. Let's see. This house
stinks. Our room stinks.


00:16:37.981 --> 00:16:39.966
- Pizza is weird here.
- Our friends are back home.


00:16:39.991 --> 00:16:42.206
And all our stuff is in the missing van.


00:16:42.231 --> 00:16:43.687
Oh, come on. It could be worse.


00:16:43.712 --> 00:16:47.256
Yeah, Joy. We could be lying
on a dirty floor. In a bag.


00:16:47.281 --> 00:16:49.375
Okay, I admit it. We had a rough start.


00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:51.415
- But think of all the good things that...
- No, Joy.


00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:54.681
There is absolutely no reason
for Riley to be happy right now.


00:16:54.706 --> 00:16:55.698
Let us handle this.


00:16:55.723 --> 00:16:58.329
I say we skip school tomorrow
and lock ourselves in the bedroom.


00:16:58.354 --> 00:17:00.034
We have no clean clothes


00:17:00.059 --> 00:17:01.841
And we could cry until we can't breathe.


00:17:01.866 --> 00:17:04.620
We should lock the door and
scream the curse word we know.


00:17:04.645 --> 00:17:06.555
- It's a good one.
- Now, hold on.


00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:09.533
Look. We all have our
off days. You know...


00:17:09.558 --> 00:17:10.594
Hi honey.


00:17:10.619 --> 00:17:14.641
The Mom bad news Train
is pulling in. Toot-toot.


00:17:14.666 --> 00:17:16.695
Still no moving van. Uh-huh.


00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.389
Now they're saying it won't be here
till Tuesday. Can you believe it.


00:17:19.414 --> 00:17:20.656
Toot-toot-toot.


00:17:20.681 --> 00:17:22.741
- Where's Dad?
- On the phone.


00:17:22.766 --> 00:17:24.709
This new adventure is
keeping him pretty busy.


00:17:24.734 --> 00:17:27.482
I rest my case.


00:17:30.157 --> 00:17:33.886
Now, for a few well
place withering scowls.


00:17:34.166 --> 00:17:36.906
I guess all I really want to say is


00:17:36.937 --> 00:17:38.284
thank you.


00:17:38.309 --> 00:17:42.735
You know. Through all these
confusion you stayed...


00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:45.627
Well, you stayed our happy girl.


00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:47.811
Your Dad is under a lot of pressure.


00:17:47.836 --> 00:17:52.137
But, if you and I can keep
smiling, it would be a big help.


00:17:52.162 --> 00:17:55.439
We can do that for him. Right?


00:17:55.469 --> 00:17:57.120
Whoa.


00:17:57.472 --> 00:17:58.976
Well.


00:18:00.195 --> 00:18:02.159
Yeah. Sure.


00:18:02.184 --> 00:18:04.892
What did we do to deserve you.


00:18:07.891 --> 00:18:10.383
- Sweet dreams.
- Good night.


00:18:11.025 --> 00:18:12.669
Well. You can't argue with Mom.


00:18:12.694 --> 00:18:13.853
- Happy it is.
- Can't argue with Mom, that's true.


00:18:13.878 --> 00:18:16.537
- Team Happy. Sounds great.
- Totally behind you, Joy.


00:18:17.294 --> 00:18:19.057
Looks like we're going into R E M.


00:18:19.082 --> 00:18:22.093
I've got dream duty so I'll take
care of sending these to long term.


00:18:22.124 --> 00:18:26.608
Great day today, guys.
All is well, team Happy.


00:18:27.524 --> 00:18:30.712
Alright. What's on
tonight, dream production?


00:18:35.742 --> 00:18:38.345
Now. This is it. The new place.


00:18:40.732 --> 00:18:43.613
Come live with me, Riley.


00:18:43.638 --> 00:18:48.440
- Somebody ordered a broccoli pizza.
- Eat me, I'm organic.


00:18:49.252 --> 00:18:52.261
Now. Who is in charge of
programming down there?


00:18:52.286 --> 00:18:55.384
I know I'm not suppose to do this. But.


00:18:59.462 --> 00:19:02.527
We are not going to
end the day like this.


00:19:45.515 --> 00:19:47.165
Don't you worry.


00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:51.249
I'm going to make sure that
tomorrow is another great day.


00:19:51.274 --> 00:19:53.431
I promise.


00:20:01.776 --> 00:20:03.719
CARAMEL CORN CURLS


00:20:05.571 --> 00:20:08.142
- Hello. Did I wake you?
- Do you have to play that?


00:20:08.167 --> 00:20:09.441
Well, I have to practice.


00:20:09.466 --> 00:20:12.889
And I don't think of it as
playing so much as hugging


00:20:12.914 --> 00:20:15.776
Okay. First day of school.
Very, very exciting.


00:20:15.801 --> 00:20:18.801
I was up late last night figuring
out a new plan. Here it is.


00:20:18.826 --> 00:20:20.053
- Fear. I need a list
- What?


00:20:20.078 --> 00:20:23.171
Of all the possible negative outcomes
on the first day at a new school.


00:20:23.196 --> 00:20:25.424
Way ahead of you there.
They won't notice no meteor.


00:20:25.449 --> 00:20:27.460
Disgust. Make sure
Riley stands out today.


00:20:27.485 --> 00:20:28.819
But, also blends in.


00:20:28.856 --> 00:20:30.786
When I'm through,
Riley will look so good,


00:20:30.811 --> 00:20:33.019
the other kids will look at
their own outfits and fart.


00:20:33.044 --> 00:20:35.646
Joy! Yes, Joy. You'll be
in charge of the console.


00:20:35.671 --> 00:20:37.093
Keeping Riley happy all day long.


00:20:37.118 --> 00:20:38.823
And may I add, I love
your dress, it's adorable.


00:20:38.848 --> 00:20:42.242
Oh, this old thing. Thank you so
much. I love the way it twirls.


00:20:42.724 --> 00:20:45.140
Train of Thought, right on schedule.


00:20:46.643 --> 00:20:48.573
Anger. Unload the daydreams.


00:20:48.598 --> 00:20:50.847
I ordered extra, in case
things get slow in class.


00:20:50.872 --> 00:20:54.163
Might come in handy. If this new school
is full of boring, useless classes.


00:20:54.188 --> 00:20:55.849
Which it probably will be.


00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:59.629
Oh, Sadness. I've a super
important job just for you.


00:20:59.654 --> 00:21:02.312
- Really. -
Uh-heh. Follow me.


00:21:03.797 --> 00:21:06.352
- What are you doing?
- And there. Perfect.


00:21:06.377 --> 00:21:08.472
This is the circle of sadness.


00:21:08.497 --> 00:21:13.064
Your job is to make sure that all
the sadness stays inside of it.


00:21:13.089 --> 00:21:15.727
So, you want me just to stand here?


00:21:15.752 --> 00:21:18.721
Hey, it's not my place to
tell you how to do your job.


00:21:18.746 --> 00:21:20.085
Just make sure that


00:21:20.116 --> 00:21:23.603
all... the sadness stays in the circle.


00:21:23.628 --> 00:21:26.789
See. You're a pro at
this. Isn't this fun?


00:21:26.814 --> 00:21:27.991
- No.
- Atta girl.


00:21:28.016 --> 00:21:29.389
Alright everyone, fresh start.


00:21:29.414 --> 00:21:31.454
We're going to have a good day
which will turn into a good week,


00:21:31.479 --> 00:21:34.149
which will turn into a good year,
which will turn into a good life!


00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:37.246
So, big day. New school. New friends.


00:21:37.271 --> 00:21:39.652
I know. I'm kind of nervous
but I'm mostly excited.


00:21:39.677 --> 00:21:42.736
- How do I look? Do you like my quote?
- Very cute.


00:21:42.761 --> 00:21:44.694
You gonna be okay. You
want us to walk with you?


00:21:44.725 --> 00:21:47.297
Mom and Dad, with us in
public. No, thank you.


00:21:47.322 --> 00:21:48.370
Yup, I'm on it.


00:21:48.395 --> 00:21:50.788
Nope, I'm fine. Bye Mom. Bye Dad.


00:21:50.813 --> 00:21:52.294
Have a good day in school, monkey.


00:21:52.319 --> 00:21:55.199
- Woo-woo... -
Woo-woot... - Woo... Woo...


00:21:57.595 --> 00:21:59.877
Have a great day, sweetheart.


00:22:05.871 --> 00:22:07.889
- Are you sure we want to do this?
- In we go.


00:22:07.914 --> 00:22:11.066
Okay, going in. Yes.


00:22:15.303 --> 00:22:17.640
Okay. We've got a group
of cool girls at 2 o'clock.


00:22:17.665 --> 00:22:20.317
- How do you know?
- Double ears pierce. Infinity scarf.


00:22:20.342 --> 00:22:23.030
- Whoa. Is she wearing eye shadow?
- Yeah. We want to be friends with them.


00:22:23.068 --> 00:22:24.487
- Let's go talk to them.
- Are you kidding.


00:22:24.512 --> 00:22:27.227
We're not talking to them.
We want them to like us.


00:22:27.252 --> 00:22:28.520
Oh... yeah. Wait. What?


00:22:28.545 --> 00:22:30.627
Almost finished with
the potential disasters.


00:22:30.652 --> 00:22:34.173
Worst scenario is either
quicksands, spontaneous combustion


00:22:34.198 --> 00:22:37.147
or getting called on by the teacher.
As long as none of those happens...


00:22:37.172 --> 00:22:39.942
Okay, everybody. We have a
new student in class today.


00:22:39.967 --> 00:22:43.383
Are you kidding me! Out of the
days! This is not happening!


00:22:43.408 --> 00:22:46.016
Riley, would you like to tell
us something about yourself?


00:22:46.041 --> 00:22:48.396
No! Pretend we can't speak English.


00:22:48.421 --> 00:22:50.453
Don't worry. I got this.


00:22:51.372 --> 00:22:52.758
Okay.


00:22:52.783 --> 00:22:54.521
My name is Riley Anderson.


00:22:54.553 --> 00:22:58.547
I'm from Minnesota and now I live here.


00:22:59.794 --> 00:23:02.219
And how about Minnesota?


00:23:02.244 --> 00:23:03.663
Can you tell us something about it?


00:23:03.688 --> 00:23:06.659
Well you certainly get a
lot more snow than we do.


00:23:07.244 --> 00:23:10.972
Ha-ha-ha.
She's hilarious.


00:23:11.575 --> 00:23:13.124
Yeah, it get's pretty cold.


00:23:13.149 --> 00:23:15.635
The lake freezes over. And
that's when we play hockey.


00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:18.068
I'm on a great team. We're
called the Prairie dogs.


00:23:18.093 --> 00:23:21.403
My friend, Mag, plays forward
and my dad's the coach.


00:23:21.428 --> 00:23:23.919
Pretty much everyone
in my family skates.


00:23:23.944 --> 00:23:25.414
It's kind of a family tradition.


00:23:25.438 --> 00:23:28.353
We go out on the lake
almost every weekend.


00:23:30.002 --> 00:23:31.825
Or, we did. Till...


00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:33.114
I moved away.


00:23:33.139 --> 00:23:34.409
- Hey. What gives?
- What?


00:23:34.434 --> 00:23:36.874
Hey, Sadness. You touched a memory.


00:23:36.899 --> 00:23:39.976
- We talked about this.
- Oh yeah, I know. But I...


00:23:40.001 --> 00:23:41.589
Get back in your circle.


00:23:41.614 --> 00:23:43.076
Ah. What's going on?


00:23:43.101 --> 00:23:45.053
- Get it out of there, Joy.
- Eject.


00:23:45.129 --> 00:23:47.529
We used to play tag and stuff.


00:23:47.554 --> 00:23:49.457
Cool kids whispering at 3 o'clock.


00:23:49.482 --> 00:23:52.340
Did you see that look?
They're judging us.


00:23:52.952 --> 00:23:55.718
Somebody help grab that
thing. Everybody put in...


00:23:55.743 --> 00:23:58.521
But, everything is different now.


00:23:58.777 --> 00:24:00.649
Since we moved.


00:24:02.243 --> 00:24:05.696
Oh no. We're crying and sloth.


00:24:05.721 --> 00:24:08.791
What? Sadness, what are you doing!


00:24:09.846 --> 00:24:12.990
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm, oh.


00:24:13.397 --> 00:24:16.921
- It's a core memory.
- But, it's blue.


00:24:17.784 --> 00:24:19.259
No! Wait!


00:24:19.284 --> 00:24:20.915
Stop it. No.


00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:22.433
No.


00:24:28.568 --> 00:24:30.003
Joy. No.


00:24:30.028 --> 00:24:31.384
- That's a core memory.
- Hey!


00:24:31.409 --> 00:24:33.379
- Stop it. Let go.
- Don't. Wait.


00:24:33.765 --> 00:24:35.713
The core memories!


00:24:39.534 --> 00:24:40.900
Aw!


00:24:49.848 --> 00:24:51.513
No-no-no...


00:24:55.633 --> 00:24:57.189
- Aw!
- Aw!


00:25:04.396 --> 00:25:05.672
Thank you, Riley.


00:25:05.697 --> 00:25:08.103
I know it can be tough
moving to a new place.


00:25:08.128 --> 00:25:10.781
But we are happy to have you here.


00:25:10.806 --> 00:25:13.068
Alright everyone. Get
out you history books.


00:25:13.093 --> 00:25:15.514
And turn to chapter 7.


00:25:17.158 --> 00:25:19.759
Can I say that curse word now?


00:25:19.784 --> 00:25:21.821
- Eh.
- Aw!


00:25:24.026 --> 00:25:25.755
Aw!


00:25:30.673 --> 00:25:34.081
Aww...!


00:25:36.692 --> 00:25:38.998
Aww...


00:25:40.095 --> 00:25:43.723
Oh no. 1, 2, 3, okay.


00:25:44.629 --> 00:25:46.968
Not enough. What?


00:25:46.992 --> 00:25:47.992
Where are we?


00:25:48.293 --> 00:25:49.992
Long term memory?


00:25:50.016 --> 00:25:51.092
What?


00:25:57.993 --> 00:25:59.092
Goof Ball Island?


00:26:00.816 --> 00:26:03.916
Riley's Island of
Personality, they're all down!


00:26:05.040 --> 00:26:07.040
Ohh... This is bad!


00:26:07.064 --> 00:26:09.064
We... we can fix this.


00:26:09.088 --> 00:26:11.088
We just have to get
back to headquarter's.


00:26:11.112 --> 00:26:13.112
Plug the core memories in...


00:26:13.136 --> 00:26:14.936
And Riley will go back to normal.


00:26:14.960 --> 00:26:17.960
Ohhh... Riley is no core memories.


00:26:17.984 --> 00:26:19.992
No personality island and no...


00:26:21.193 --> 00:26:22.292
What? What is it?


00:26:22.916 --> 00:26:23.916
You.


00:26:23.940 --> 00:26:25.940
You're not in headquarter's.


00:26:25.964 --> 00:26:28.064
Without you Riley can't be happy.


00:26:28.788 --> 00:26:30.788
We gotta get you back up there.


00:26:31.412 --> 00:26:32.912
I'm coming Riley.


00:28:10.993 --> 00:28:14.787
What a nice pass, over to
Reed. Constance cross the line.


00:28:17.844 --> 00:28:20.034
Uh-oh. She's looking at us.


00:28:20.586 --> 00:28:21.979
- What did she say?
- What?


00:28:22.004 --> 00:28:23.863
Oh, sorry sir. No one was listening.


00:28:23.888 --> 00:28:26.229
Isn't it garbage night?
We let the toilet seat up.


00:28:26.254 --> 00:28:28.385
What? What is it, woman? What?


00:28:28.410 --> 00:28:32.450
- He's making that stupid face again.
- I could strangle him right now.


00:28:32.475 --> 00:28:34.674
Signal him again.


00:28:36.091 --> 00:28:37.651
Ah. So.


00:28:37.676 --> 00:28:39.014
Riley, how was school?


00:28:39.039 --> 00:28:40.904
- Aw. Waste of time. - You got
to be kidding me. - Seriously?


00:28:40.929 --> 00:28:44.292
For this, we gave up that
Brazilian helicopter pilot?


00:28:44.317 --> 00:28:46.175
Move! I'll be joy.


00:28:46.200 --> 00:28:48.261
School was great. Alright.


00:28:48.286 --> 00:28:50.826
Riley. Is everything okay?


00:28:51.755 --> 00:28:53.540
Sir, she just rolled her eyes at us.


00:28:53.565 --> 00:28:54.897
What is her deal?


00:28:54.929 --> 00:28:58.267
Alright, make a show of force. I don't
want to have to put the foot down.


00:28:58.292 --> 00:29:00.214
No. Not the foot.


00:29:00.239 --> 00:29:02.628
Riley, I do not like this new attitude.


00:29:02.653 --> 00:29:04.382
Oh. I'll show you attitude, old man.


00:29:04.407 --> 00:29:05.860
No-no-no-no.
Stay happy.


00:29:06.416 --> 00:29:08.695
What is your problem?
Just leave me alone.


00:29:08.720 --> 00:29:10.900
Sir. Reporting high level of sass.


00:29:10.925 --> 00:29:12.510
Take it to DEFCON 2.


00:29:12.535 --> 00:29:15.233
Your heard that gentlemen. DEFCON 2.


00:29:15.757 --> 00:29:19.365
Listen, young lady. I don't know where
this disrespectful attitude came from.


00:29:19.390 --> 00:29:22.252
You want a piece of this,
pops. Come and get it!


00:29:22.277 --> 00:29:24.024
Yeah. Well. Well.


00:29:24.049 --> 00:29:27.057
Here it comes. Prepare the foot.


00:29:27.762 --> 00:29:29.894
Keys, to exec position.


00:29:31.084 --> 00:29:33.621
Ready to launch on your command, sir.


00:29:34.189 --> 00:29:35.570
AW!


00:29:35.595 --> 00:29:37.474
Just, shut up!


00:29:38.175 --> 00:29:39.659
Fire.


00:29:39.684 --> 00:29:41.917
That's it. Go to your room.


00:29:42.342 --> 00:29:44.120
Now.


00:29:46.751 --> 00:29:50.336
Foot is down. The foot is down.


00:29:50.850 --> 00:29:54.872
Good job, gentlemen. That
could've been a disaster.


00:29:54.913 --> 00:29:57.025
Well, that was a disaster.


00:29:59.932 --> 00:30:03.567
Come. Fly with me, criancinha. (baby)


00:30:03.679 --> 00:30:05.597
- Ah.
- Ahh.


00:30:14.796 --> 00:30:17.919
We're gonna walk out there, on that?


00:30:17.944 --> 00:30:19.617
It's the quickest way back.


00:30:19.655 --> 00:30:24.234
But it's right over the Memory Dump.
If we fall, we'll be forgotten forever.


00:30:24.259 --> 00:30:26.116
We have to do this for Riley.


00:30:26.141 --> 00:30:28.408
Just follow my footsteps.


00:30:28.433 --> 00:30:31.608
Not that high. It's totally, ah.


00:30:39.438 --> 00:30:41.514
Wooah.


00:30:47.702 --> 00:30:49.257
Hey.


00:30:49.430 --> 00:30:50.970
So...


00:30:50.995 --> 00:30:53.654
Things got a little
out of hand downstairs.


00:30:53.679 --> 00:30:55.790
You wanna talk about it?


00:30:56.606 --> 00:30:59.581
Come on. Where's my happy girl?


00:31:00.712 --> 00:31:02.522
Monkey. Woo-hoo.


00:31:02.547 --> 00:31:05.497
Whoa! He's trying to start up Goofball.


00:31:05.921 --> 00:31:09.265
Come on. Hoo-Haa.


00:31:19.546 --> 00:31:21.592
Sadness! Turn right back!


00:31:49.135 --> 00:31:50.809
What the?


00:32:05.724 --> 00:32:09.562
I get it. You need some alone time.


00:32:11.289 --> 00:32:13.242
And we'll talk later.


00:32:16.303 --> 00:32:20.827
- We have a major problem.
- Oh, Joy. Where are you?


00:32:21.232 --> 00:32:23.873
We lost Goofball Island.


00:32:23.898 --> 00:32:28.792
That means she can lose Friendship
and Hockey and Honesty and Family.


00:32:28.817 --> 00:32:31.184
You can fixed this. Right, Joy?


00:32:31.209 --> 00:32:34.784
- I-I don't
know. - Oh.


00:32:34.809 --> 00:32:37.662
But we have to try. Okay, come on.


00:32:38.475 --> 00:32:40.473
- Riley's gone to sleep.
- Oh.


00:32:40.498 --> 00:32:43.853
Which is a good thing If...
When you think about it.


00:32:43.878 --> 00:32:46.629
Because nothing else bad
can happen when she's asleep.


00:32:46.655 --> 00:32:48.828
We'll be back to Headquarters
before she wakes up.


00:32:48.853 --> 00:32:52.255
We'll just go across Friendship Island.


00:32:53.686 --> 00:32:56.200
- Oh, we'll never
make it. - No-no-no...


00:32:56.229 --> 00:32:57.938
Don't obsess over the
way of life's problems


00:32:57.963 --> 00:33:00.036
Remember the funny
movie where the dog dies.


00:33:00.061 --> 00:33:02.571
Oh Sadness. We don't have time for this.


00:33:02.596 --> 00:33:04.456
We'll just have to go around.


00:33:04.481 --> 00:33:06.136
Take the scenic route.


00:33:06.161 --> 00:33:08.681
Wait. Joy, you can get lost in there.


00:33:08.857 --> 00:33:11.123
- Think positive.
- Okay.


00:33:11.148 --> 00:33:14.390
I'm positive you will get lost in there.


00:33:14.415 --> 00:33:16.333
That's long term memory.


00:33:16.358 --> 00:33:18.674
An endless swarm of
corridors and shelves.


00:33:18.699 --> 00:33:21.387
I read about it in the manuals.


00:33:21.412 --> 00:33:24.308
The manuals? The manuals.


00:33:24.333 --> 00:33:26.081
- You read the manuals.
- Yeah.


00:33:26.106 --> 00:33:28.328
So you know the way
back to headquarters.


00:33:28.353 --> 00:33:32.605
- I guess.
- Woo-Hnn!


00:33:32.630 --> 00:33:33.961
You are my map.


00:33:33.986 --> 00:33:36.219
Let's go. Lead on, my map.


00:33:36.244 --> 00:33:37.391
Show me where we're going.


00:33:37.416 --> 00:33:39.386
Okay, only.


00:33:39.411 --> 00:33:41.144
I'm too sad to walk.


00:33:41.169 --> 00:33:45.671
Just give me a few hours to...


00:33:45.907 --> 00:33:48.704
- Which way, left?
- Right.


00:33:48.745 --> 00:33:52.275
No, I mean go left. I said
left was right like correct.


00:33:52.303 --> 00:33:53.342
Okay.


00:33:53.374 --> 00:33:55.646
This actually feels kind of nice.


00:33:55.671 --> 00:33:59.490
Okay, here we go. We'll be back
to Headquarters before morning.


00:33:59.515 --> 00:34:01.542
We can do it. This will be easy!


00:34:01.567 --> 00:34:04.028
This is working.


00:34:06.279 --> 00:34:07.642
This is not working.


00:34:07.675 --> 00:34:11.405
- Are we getting close?
- Yeah. Just another right.


00:34:11.430 --> 00:34:15.618
And a left. And then another left.


00:34:15.643 --> 00:34:18.536
Are you sure you know where we're going?


00:34:18.561 --> 00:34:21.937
'Cause we seem to be walking
away from Headquarters.


00:34:21.962 --> 00:34:24.291
Oh. Riley's awake.


00:34:24.854 --> 00:34:26.936
Oh. Oh. uh.


00:34:28.023 --> 00:34:29.749
Don't. Don't touch, remember?


00:34:29.774 --> 00:34:32.356
If you touch them, they stay sad.


00:34:32.381 --> 00:34:34.700
Oh. Sorry. I... I won't.


00:34:34.745 --> 00:34:38.333
- Starting now.
- I can't take much more of this.


00:34:38.358 --> 00:34:39.905
Forget them!


00:34:39.930 --> 00:34:43.590
- Mind workers.
- But, Joy, we're almost oh.


00:34:43.615 --> 00:34:45.466
Phone numbers. We don't need all these.


00:34:45.494 --> 00:34:46.466
They're in her phone.


00:34:46.491 --> 00:34:47.814
- Just forget all that, please.
- Excuse me. Hi.


00:34:47.839 --> 00:34:50.076
Forget it.


00:34:50.101 --> 00:34:53.307
- I need to find Friendship Island.
- Look at this. 4 years of piano lessons.


00:34:53.332 --> 00:34:54.398
Yeah. It looks pretty faded.


00:34:54.423 --> 00:34:57.572
You know what. Save Chopsticks and
Heart and Soul, get rid of the rest.


00:34:57.826 --> 00:34:59.720
- Are you.
- US presidents. What do you think?


00:34:59.745 --> 00:35:01.619
Just keep Washington,
Lincoln and the fat one.


00:35:01.644 --> 00:35:02.984
- Forget them!
- Hey!


00:35:03.009 --> 00:35:05.540
You can't throw those away.
Those are perfectly good memories.


00:35:05.565 --> 00:35:07.963
The names of every
Cutiepie princess doll?


00:35:08.007 --> 00:35:09.914
Yes. That is critical information.


00:35:09.939 --> 00:35:12.723
- Glitter storm, Honey pants...
- Forget them.


00:35:17.250 --> 00:35:19.089
- Hey! Bring those back.
- They're in the Dump.


00:35:19.114 --> 00:35:22.411
- Nothing comes back from the Dump.
- Yeah. Look, lady. This is our job, okay.


00:35:22.436 --> 00:35:24.619
When Riley doesn't care
about a memory, it fades.


00:35:24.644 --> 00:35:26.202
- Fades?
- Happens to the best of them.


00:35:26.227 --> 00:35:30.564
Except for this bad boy.
This one will never fade


00:35:32.178 --> 00:35:33.644
The song from the gum commercial?


00:35:33.668 --> 00:35:35.908
You know. Sometimes we send that
one up to Headquarters for no reason.


00:35:35.934 --> 00:35:40.312
It just plays in Rileys head over
and over again like a million times.


00:35:40.337 --> 00:35:42.599
Let's watch it again.


00:35:43.126 --> 00:35:46.120
Yeah, I know. We all know
the song. Okay, real catchy.


00:35:46.145 --> 00:35:48.559
- Hey. What do you think, should we do it?
- Yeah.


00:35:48.584 --> 00:35:52.735
Okay. Here we
go! Ha-ha-ha.


00:35:54.191 --> 00:35:56.127
What the? This again?


00:35:56.152 --> 00:35:57.337
Ha. Great.


00:35:57.362 --> 00:36:00.675
Wait! Do you know how to
get to Friendship Island!


00:36:00.980 --> 00:36:03.364
Do you like it there? Did
you feel any earthquakes?


00:36:03.389 --> 00:36:04.553
Is the bridge cool?


00:36:04.578 --> 00:36:06.978
Yes. Good. What happened
with the playoffs.


00:36:07.003 --> 00:36:10.367
We won the first game. Coach says we
might actually go to the finals this year.


00:36:10.392 --> 00:36:13.456
Oh, and we got this new girl
on the team. She's so cool.


00:36:13.481 --> 00:36:15.990
- Uh. She did not just say that.
- A new girl?


00:36:16.015 --> 00:36:18.201
Mag has a new friend already?


00:36:18.226 --> 00:36:19.523
Hey-hey. Stay happy.


00:36:19.548 --> 00:36:21.755
We do not want to lose
anymore islands here, guys.


00:36:21.780 --> 00:36:24.019
We can pass the puck to each
other without even looking.


00:36:24.044 --> 00:36:25.509
It's like mind reading.


00:36:25.534 --> 00:36:26.901
You like to read minds, Mag.


00:36:26.926 --> 00:36:28.141
- I got something for you to read.
- Anger. What?


00:36:28.179 --> 00:36:30.151
- Right here! - Wait-wait-wait.
Let's just be calm for 1 second.


00:36:30.177 --> 00:36:31.591
Aw!


00:36:31.818 --> 00:36:33.222
- I got to got.
- What?


00:36:33.247 --> 00:36:35.081
I got to go.


00:36:35.520 --> 00:36:38.933
Wait. Could you just
please tell me which way is.


00:36:38.958 --> 00:36:40.609
Oh no.


00:36:43.013 --> 00:36:45.473
Friendship Island. What?


00:36:56.678 --> 00:36:58.776
Not Friendship.


00:37:03.673 --> 00:37:08.634
Oh, Riley love that
one. And now it's gone.


00:37:08.659 --> 00:37:12.829
Goodbye Friendship Hello Loneliness.


00:37:16.057 --> 00:37:18.765
We'll just have to go the long way.


00:37:18.790 --> 00:37:24.527
Yeah. The long long long... way.


00:37:24.552 --> 00:37:26.569
I'm ready.


00:37:27.343 --> 00:37:30.279
There's got to be a better way.


00:37:31.511 --> 00:37:34.401
- Woo. Well look at you.
- Huh?


00:37:34.426 --> 00:37:37.129
I will take you but not you.


00:37:37.154 --> 00:37:39.563
Ah! Who am I kidding. I can't leave you.


00:37:39.595 --> 00:37:40.938
Hello!


00:37:40.963 --> 00:37:43.452
- Aw.
- Wait. Hey, wait.


00:37:44.897 --> 00:37:46.778
No, wait. Stop.


00:37:55.110 --> 00:37:57.021
- Excuse me.
- Aw!


00:37:58.046 --> 00:37:59.881
Oh. I was, I was looking for


00:37:59.906 --> 00:38:01.202
- diversion!
- What?


00:38:01.227 --> 00:38:03.725
Ha ha! So long, sucker.


00:38:04.283 --> 00:38:05.492
Ou. I'm hurt all over.


00:38:05.517 --> 00:38:07.155
Wait, I know you.


00:38:07.180 --> 00:38:09.575
No, you don't. I get that a lot.


00:38:09.600 --> 00:38:12.479
- I look like a lot of people.
- No no no... I do.


00:38:12.504 --> 00:38:15.277
Bing Bong, Riley's imaginary friend.


00:38:15.302 --> 00:38:17.765
- You really do know me?
- Of course.


00:38:17.790 --> 00:38:20.462
Riley loved playings with
you. You two were best friends.


00:38:20.487 --> 00:38:21.836
Oh, oh. You wouldn't know.


00:38:21.861 --> 00:38:24.028
- We're trying to get back to Headquarters.
- Headquarters?


00:38:24.053 --> 00:38:26.682
- You guys are from Headquarters?
- Well, yeah.


00:38:26.707 --> 00:38:28.196
I'm Joy. This is Sadness.


00:38:28.221 --> 00:38:30.254
- You're Joy,
the Joy? - Uh-huh.


00:38:30.279 --> 00:38:31.896
What the heck are you doing out here?


00:38:31.920 --> 00:38:34.695
That's a good question. You
want to answer that, Sadness?


00:38:34.721 --> 00:38:37.455
Without you, I won't ever be happy.


00:38:37.480 --> 00:38:39.483
We can't have that.
We got to get you back.


00:38:39.508 --> 00:38:41.532
I'll tell you what. Follow me.


00:38:41.707 --> 00:38:44.305
Thank you. It is so
great to see you again.


00:38:44.330 --> 00:38:46.785
I got to tell you. I'm such
a huge fan of your work.


00:38:46.810 --> 00:38:49.251
Do you remember when you
and Riley were in a band?


00:38:49.276 --> 00:38:51.659
Ha-ha-ha. I went to
all of your concerts.


00:38:51.684 --> 00:38:53.095
Yeah. I blow a mean nose.


00:38:53.120 --> 00:38:55.987
- Watching you play tag was such a treat.
- 2 time room champ.


00:38:56.012 --> 00:39:00.265
- Oh, and remember your rockets.
- Of course, it runs on song power.


00:39:00.290 --> 00:39:01.727
That's right. Your theme song.


00:39:01.758 --> 00:39:04.409
- Who's your friend who likes to play?
- Bing Bong. Bing Bong.


00:39:04.434 --> 00:39:07.912
- His rocket makes you yell "Hooray!"
- Bing Bong. Bing Bong.


00:39:07.937 --> 00:39:10.275
What exactly are you suppose to be?


00:39:10.300 --> 00:39:13.307
You know what's unclear?
I'm mostly cotton candy. But.


00:39:13.338 --> 00:39:17.887
Shape wise. I'm part cat,
part elephant, part dolphin.


00:39:17.912 --> 00:39:19.539
Dolphin?


00:39:21.756 --> 00:39:24.796
You got to remember. When Riley
was 3, animals were all her age.


00:39:24.821 --> 00:39:26.725
The cow goes moo. The horse goes neigh.


00:39:26.750 --> 00:39:28.207
It's all the people talked back then.


00:39:28.232 --> 00:39:29.815
Yeah, yeah. I guess that true.


00:39:29.840 --> 00:39:31.271
- What are you doing out here?
- Well.


00:39:31.296 --> 00:39:34.490
There's not much call for
imaginary friends lately.


00:39:34.515 --> 00:39:38.280
So, I. You know...


00:39:38.578 --> 00:39:41.002
Yeah, yeah, Don't be sad.


00:39:41.027 --> 00:39:43.103
Tell you what. When I get
back up to Headquarters.


00:39:43.128 --> 00:39:45.415
I'll make sure Riley remembers you.


00:39:45.440 --> 00:39:47.845
- You will?
- Of course. She loved that.


00:39:47.870 --> 00:39:51.903
Ha-ha! This is the
greatest day of my life.


00:39:52.576 --> 00:39:55.156
Aw aw aw...


00:39:55.437 --> 00:39:58.241
- Are you okay?
- Hey, what's going on?


00:39:58.266 --> 00:39:59.600
I cry candy.


00:39:59.625 --> 00:40:02.336
- Try the caramel, it's delicious.
- Woo.


00:40:02.361 --> 00:40:03.787
- Whoa!
- Woo.


00:40:03.812 --> 00:40:05.385
- Here use this.
- Thanks.


00:40:05.410 --> 00:40:07.413
Oh, hold on. Wait a second.


00:40:09.949 --> 00:40:12.933
It always get stuck at the bottom.


00:40:14.708 --> 00:40:16.177
Here.


00:40:16.208 --> 00:40:17.919
What? It's imaginary.


00:40:17.944 --> 00:40:20.908
Thanks. This will make it a lot
easier to walk back to Headquarters.


00:40:20.933 --> 00:40:22.594
Walk? We're not walking.


00:40:22.619 --> 00:40:26.234
We're taking the Train of Thought.


00:40:26.533 --> 00:40:28.384
The Train. Of course.


00:40:28.409 --> 00:40:31.030
That is so much fast.
But how do we catch it.


00:40:31.055 --> 00:40:35.499
Well, it kind of go all over the place
but there is a station in Imagination Land.


00:40:35.524 --> 00:40:38.103
I know a shortcut. Come on, this way.


00:40:38.128 --> 00:40:40.810
Oh. I'm so glad we ran into you.


00:40:40.835 --> 00:40:43.627
The station is right in here. After you.


00:40:43.652 --> 00:40:45.132
- Joy.
- What?


00:40:45.157 --> 00:40:48.405
Well. I read about this place in
the manual. We shouldn't go in there.


00:40:48.430 --> 00:40:50.347
Bing Bong says it's the
quickest way to Headquarters.


00:40:50.378 --> 00:40:52.582
No. But Joy, this is abstract thought.


00:40:52.607 --> 00:40:54.943
What are you talking about?
I go in here all the time.


00:40:54.968 --> 00:40:56.728
It's a shortcut. You see.


00:40:56.759 --> 00:40:59.420
[DANGER
- KEEP OUT!] D A N G E R. Shortcut.


00:40:59.445 --> 00:41:01.251
I'll prove it to you.


00:41:01.464 --> 00:41:02.772
Look at me.


00:41:02.797 --> 00:41:06.838
I'm crossing into the station.
'Cause I'm taking the shortcut.


00:41:06.863 --> 00:41:08.687
Let's. Let's go around. This way.


00:41:08.712 --> 00:41:11.110
Almost there.


00:41:11.361 --> 00:41:13.877
If you want to walk
the long way, go for it.


00:41:13.902 --> 00:41:17.601
But Riley needs to be happy.
I'm not missing that Train.


00:41:17.626 --> 00:41:21.083
Bing Bong knows what he is doing.
He's part dolphin, they're very smart.


00:41:21.108 --> 00:41:23.611
Well, I guess.


00:41:41.459 --> 00:41:45.426
Okay. What abstract concept are
we trying to comprehend today.


00:41:45.451 --> 00:41:47.009
- Loneliness.
- Hm.


00:41:47.034 --> 00:41:48.671
I think there is something in there.


00:41:48.702 --> 00:41:51.266
I'm going to turn it on for a minute
and burn out the dumb thoughts.


00:41:51.291 --> 00:41:54.299
What did I tell ya. You'll
be in Headquarters in no time.


00:41:55.088 --> 00:41:57.062
Hey, will you look at that?


00:41:57.087 --> 00:42:00.182
- Whoa. What's happening?
- Oh no, they turned it on.


00:42:00.207 --> 00:42:02.893
Oh. Never seen this before.


00:42:05.041 --> 00:42:08.307
My face. My beautiful face. Whoa!


00:42:08.332 --> 00:42:10.128
- What is going on?
- We're abstracting.


00:42:10.153 --> 00:42:12.198
There are 4 stages. This is the first.


00:42:12.223 --> 00:42:14.176
Nonobjective fragmentation.


00:42:14.201 --> 00:42:18.282
Alright, do not panic. What's
important is that we all stay together.


00:42:18.307 --> 00:42:19.313
- Oh.
- Aw.


00:42:19.338 --> 00:42:22.078
We're in the second stage.
We're deconstructing.


00:42:22.103 --> 00:42:23.693
Run!


00:42:23.718 --> 00:42:27.081
Aw. I can't feel my legs.


00:42:27.106 --> 00:42:29.847
- Oh, there they are.
- Come here, me.


00:42:31.114 --> 00:42:35.058
We got to get out of here. Before
we're not even shape and color


00:42:35.083 --> 00:42:36.823
We'll get stuck here forever


00:42:36.848 --> 00:42:38.544
Bong. Why did we come in here?


00:42:38.569 --> 00:42:41.455
I told you. It's a shortcut.


00:42:41.480 --> 00:42:43.053
The Train.


00:42:46.783 --> 00:42:50.488
Oh no. We're 2
dimensional. That's stage 3.


00:42:50.513 --> 00:42:53.181
- We're getting no where.
- Death. Unlucky death.


00:42:53.206 --> 00:42:54.764
Come on.


00:42:57.525 --> 00:42:59.219
We can't fit.


00:42:59.244 --> 00:43:02.826
Oh no, we're not figurative
This is the last stage.


00:43:02.851 --> 00:43:04.952
We're not gonna make it.


00:43:06.600 --> 00:43:10.675
Wait, we're 2 dimensional.
Fall on your face.


00:43:20.768 --> 00:43:23.652
Stop. Stop!


00:43:24.951 --> 00:43:27.158
No. You said that was a shortcut.


00:43:27.228 --> 00:43:30.284
I did. But wow, we should
not had gone in there.


00:43:30.309 --> 00:43:32.552
That was dangerous. They
should really put up a sign.


00:43:32.577 --> 00:43:34.822
- How long till the next Train?
- Who knows?


00:43:34.847 --> 00:43:37.405
But don't worry. There's
another station. That way.


00:43:37.430 --> 00:43:40.688
The Train always stops there, right
before it goes to Headquarters.


00:43:40.713 --> 00:43:42.712
If we hurry, we can catch it.


00:43:42.737 --> 00:43:44.926
This isn't another one
of your shortcuts, is it?


00:43:44.951 --> 00:43:47.566
Ha-ha-ha.
Yeah.


00:43:47.591 --> 00:43:51.290
- Is there really another
station? - Uh-huh. Through there.


00:43:52.756 --> 00:43:57.265
- Welcome to Imagination Land.
- Imagination Land?


00:43:57.290 --> 00:43:59.956
Sure. I come here all the
time. I'm practically the mayor.


00:43:59.993 --> 00:44:03.625
Hey, you guys hungry?
There's French Fries Forest.


00:44:03.826 --> 00:44:05.814
No way!
Ha-ha-ha.


00:44:05.839 --> 00:44:08.147
Check it out. Trophy Town.


00:44:08.174 --> 00:44:11.916
Medals, Ribbons. Everyone's a winner.


00:44:11.941 --> 00:44:13.547
I won first prize.


00:44:13.572 --> 00:44:16.594
- Me too!
- Oh. Participation award.


00:44:16.619 --> 00:44:18.517
Wait, is that? Is that a? Look.


00:44:18.542 --> 00:44:20.212
It's Cloud Town.


00:44:20.237 --> 00:44:22.119
That's my favorite.
Hoo-hoo-hoo.


00:44:22.144 --> 00:44:25.063
- Oh, it's so soft.
- Oh oh oh. Let me try.


00:44:25.088 --> 00:44:27.160
Hey! What the big idea?


00:44:27.185 --> 00:44:30.939
You better fix that wall or
else you're in big trouble.


00:44:31.829 --> 00:44:34.936
Oh no, lava. Woo. Whoa.


00:44:34.961 --> 00:44:37.911
Imagination Land is the best.


00:44:38.135 --> 00:44:40.972
Oh, is it all going
to be so interactive.


00:44:40.997 --> 00:44:43.182
Hey look! The House of Cards.


00:44:43.207 --> 00:44:45.818
Woo wait. Hang on just a minute.


00:44:45.843 --> 00:44:47.150
- Your rocket.
- Yeah.


00:44:47.175 --> 00:44:48.990
I stashed it in there for safekeeping.


00:44:49.015 --> 00:44:52.507
And now I'm all set to
take Riley to the moon!


00:44:52.532 --> 00:44:54.553
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Great.


00:44:54.578 --> 00:44:57.553
- Whoa. I love Imagination Land.
- Isn't it great?


00:44:57.578 --> 00:44:59.928
And there's always something new like...


00:45:02.196 --> 00:45:05.066
- Who the heck is that?
- Imaginary boyfriend.


00:45:05.091 --> 00:45:07.367
- I would die for Riley.
- Whoa.


00:45:07.392 --> 00:45:10.427
- I've never seen him before.
- I live in Canada.


00:45:10.452 --> 00:45:14.245
Anyway. Through Preschool
World. We're nearly to the train.


00:45:14.270 --> 00:45:17.825
Riley, here we come.
Woo-Hoo. Ha-ha-ha.


00:45:18.234 --> 00:45:21.961
This should be fun.
New team. New friends.


00:45:21.986 --> 00:45:23.361
There kids looked pretty good.


00:45:23.386 --> 00:45:26.381
Considering they're from
San Francisco. Heh-heh-heh.


00:45:26.406 --> 00:45:29.472
- Got to go.
- Okay. Good luck, sweetie.


00:45:29.501 --> 00:45:32.588
Look, kissing isn't going to help us now. If
she tries to use Hockey Island. It's going down.


00:45:32.613 --> 00:45:36.254
Which is why, I recalled every
hockey memory I can think of.


00:45:36.279 --> 00:45:38.851
One of these is got to work
in place of a core memory.


00:45:38.876 --> 00:45:41.562
- She's about to play.
- Hurry.


00:45:47.129 --> 00:45:50.700
Ha ha. We did it gang. It's working.


00:45:50.725 --> 00:45:52.233
Oh.


00:46:02.262 --> 00:46:05.078
Hahaha.
No-no-no... Aw!


00:46:09.616 --> 00:46:12.019
It's like we don't learn anything.


00:46:18.232 --> 00:46:19.461
- That's it.
- No no no.


00:46:19.486 --> 00:46:21.309
Free on your happy place.


00:46:21.940 --> 00:46:23.931
Aw!


00:46:33.416 --> 00:46:35.404
- Riley, what's wrong?
- Let's go.


00:46:35.429 --> 00:46:37.570
- You're not going to finish try outs?
- What's the point?


00:46:37.595 --> 00:46:39.719
Hey. It will be alright.


00:46:39.744 --> 00:46:42.887
- Let's just go back.
- Stop saying everything will be alright.


00:46:54.420 --> 00:46:56.242
Hockey!


00:46:58.165 --> 00:47:00.835
Oh no no. She loves hockey.


00:47:00.860 --> 00:47:03.340
She can't give up hockey.


00:47:05.161 --> 00:47:06.827
Bing Bong, we have to
get to that station.


00:47:06.852 --> 00:47:09.327
Sure thing. This way, just
past Grand Cracker Castle.


00:47:09.352 --> 00:47:11.070
Hey. That's weird.


00:47:11.095 --> 00:47:14.302
Grand Cracker Castle used to be right
here. I wonder why they moved it.


00:47:15.089 --> 00:47:17.621
I would have sworn Sparkle
Pointy Mountain was right here.


00:47:17.646 --> 00:47:19.240
- Hey, what's going on?
- Yeah yeah. I don't know.


00:47:19.265 --> 00:47:22.301
- We'll have to come back.
- Princess Dreamworld


00:47:23.938 --> 00:47:27.534
Oh, The Stuffed Animal Hall of Fame.


00:47:28.708 --> 00:47:30.238
My rocket?


00:47:30.263 --> 00:47:33.185
Wait. Riley and I were
still using that rocket.


00:47:33.337 --> 00:47:35.123
It still has some song power left.


00:47:35.148 --> 00:47:37.546
Who's your friend who likes to play?


00:47:42.961 --> 00:47:44.963
No! No no.


00:47:44.988 --> 00:47:49.277
You can't take my rocket to the Dump.
Riley and I are going to the moon.


00:47:54.167 --> 00:47:57.020
Riley can't be done with me?


00:48:02.414 --> 00:48:05.970
Hey, it's going to be
okay. We can fix this.


00:48:05.995 --> 00:48:09.408
We just need to get back to Headquarters.
Which way to the Train station?


00:48:09.433 --> 00:48:12.898
I had a whole trip planned for us.


00:48:13.179 --> 00:48:18.548
Hey, who's ticklish. Here
comes the tickle monster.


00:48:19.274 --> 00:48:21.201
Hey. Bing Bong, look at this.


00:48:23.709 --> 00:48:26.428
Oh, here's a fun game. You
point to the Train station


00:48:26.453 --> 00:48:30.222
and we all go there. Won't that be fun?


00:48:30.247 --> 00:48:32.872
Come on, let's go to the Train station.


00:48:34.122 --> 00:48:36.801
I'm sorry they took your rocket.


00:48:36.864 --> 00:48:41.473
They took something that you
loved. It's gone, forever.


00:48:41.498 --> 00:48:44.593
- Sadness, don't make him feel worse.
- Sorry.


00:48:44.618 --> 00:48:47.055
It's all I had left with Riley.


00:48:47.080 --> 00:48:49.979
I bet you and Riley
had great adventures.


00:48:50.004 --> 00:48:52.052
Oh, they were wonderful.


00:48:52.077 --> 00:48:56.137
Once, we flew back in time. We
had breakfast twice that day.


00:48:56.162 --> 00:49:00.221
- Sadness.
- It sounds amazing. I bet Riley liked it.


00:49:00.246 --> 00:49:04.494
Oh, she did. We were best friends.


00:49:04.519 --> 00:49:07.473
Yeah. Yeah.


00:49:12.173 --> 00:49:13.729
What?


00:49:19.046 --> 00:49:20.823
I'm okay now.


00:49:21.936 --> 00:49:25.651
Come on. The Train station is this way.


00:49:31.297 --> 00:49:33.568
- How did you do that?
- Oh, I don't know.


00:49:33.593 --> 00:49:36.917
- I feel sad so I listen to what...
- Hey!


00:49:36.942 --> 00:49:39.113
There's the Train.


00:49:49.048 --> 00:49:53.827
Oh, we made it. We're
finally going to get home.


00:49:53.852 --> 00:49:57.611
Oh no. These facts and
opinions look so similar.


00:49:57.636 --> 00:50:00.708
Don't worry about it.
Happens all the time.


00:50:04.221 --> 00:50:07.035
On a scale of 1 to 10.
I give this day an 'F'.


00:50:07.060 --> 00:50:09.934
Well, why don't we quit
standing around and do something.


00:50:09.959 --> 00:50:13.243
- Like what, genius?
- Like quitting. That's what I'm doing.


00:50:13.268 --> 00:50:18.368
Sure. It's the coward's way out.
But this coward is gonna survive.


00:50:25.091 --> 00:50:27.396
Emotions can't quit, genius.


00:50:27.995 --> 00:50:31.269
Ewg. I thought we're
suppose to keep Riley happy


00:50:31.298 --> 00:50:33.806
Wait a minute. Wait a minute!


00:50:36.189 --> 00:50:38.713
Uh-huh! HO ho ho...


00:50:38.738 --> 00:50:40.325
- What is it?
- Oh nothing.


00:50:40.350 --> 00:50:42.588
- Just the best idea ever.
- What?


00:50:42.613 --> 00:50:45.321
All the good core memories
were made in Minnesota.


00:50:45.346 --> 00:50:48.436
Ergo, we go back to
Minnesota and make more.


00:50:48.461 --> 00:50:49.596
- Ta-dah. -
Wait wait wait.


00:50:49.621 --> 00:50:51.607
You're say we run away?


00:50:51.632 --> 00:50:53.026
Well, I wouldn't call it that.


00:50:53.051 --> 00:50:55.861
I call it the 'Happy core
memory development program'.


00:50:55.886 --> 00:50:58.466
- You can't be serious.
- Hey, our life was perfect.


00:50:58.491 --> 00:51:02.703
Until Mon and Dad decided
to move to San Fran stincko.


00:51:02.728 --> 00:51:04.729
But, I mean. It's just so drastic.


00:51:04.754 --> 00:51:07.245
Need I remind you of how
great things were there.


00:51:07.270 --> 00:51:11.031
Our room. Our backyard. Our friends.


00:51:13.302 --> 00:51:15.751
Did I ask for the gum commercial?


00:51:15.776 --> 00:51:17.310
Anyway, it was better. That's my point.


00:51:17.335 --> 00:51:20.730
- Yeah, Riley was happier in Minnesota.
- Wait. Hold on.


00:51:20.755 --> 00:51:22.415
Should we just sleep
on this or something?


00:51:22.440 --> 00:51:23.925
Fine, let's sleep on it.


00:51:23.950 --> 00:51:30.204
But, hey. I'm sure joyly fun-filled
times are just around the corner.


00:51:35.932 --> 00:51:37.251
Huh?


00:51:41.329 --> 00:51:42.960
Hey hey. Why aren't we moving?


00:51:42.985 --> 00:51:45.447
Riley's gone to sleep.
We're all on break.


00:51:45.472 --> 00:51:47.298
You mean we're stuck here until morning?


00:51:47.323 --> 00:51:49.423
Yeah. The Train of Thought
doesn't run while she's asleep.


00:51:49.452 --> 00:51:52.120
- Oh, we can't wait that long.
- How about we wake her up.


00:51:52.145 --> 00:51:55.806
Sadness, that's ridiculous.
How can we possibly...


00:51:57.308 --> 00:51:59.626
- How about we wake her up.
- Great idea Joy.


00:51:59.651 --> 00:52:01.183
Thanks, come on.


00:52:01.208 --> 00:52:03.214
PRODUCTION OF Dreams


00:52:05.570 --> 00:52:07.935
Whoa. This place is huge.


00:52:07.960 --> 00:52:10.851
It looks so much
smaller than I expected.


00:52:10.876 --> 00:52:15.435
Wow, I can fly. I love that one.


00:52:15.956 --> 00:52:18.696
Rainbow Unicorn. She's right there.


00:52:21.086 --> 00:52:23.007
My friend says you're famous.


00:52:23.032 --> 00:52:24.935
- She wants your autograph.
- No no, Sadness.


00:52:24.964 --> 00:52:26.847
Don't bother Miss. Unicorn, okay?


00:52:26.876 --> 00:52:30.711
Sorry she's from out of town.
It's so embarrassing, right?


00:52:31.203 --> 00:52:35.257
I love you in Fairy Dream Adventure
part 7. Okay bye. I love you.


00:52:35.301 --> 00:52:36.512
[NO ENTRY WHEN THE LIGHT IS ON]


00:52:36.537 --> 00:52:40.249
Huh! Wonder what that
means? Oh well, let's go in.


00:52:41.632 --> 00:52:43.297
Set up the classroom set.


00:52:43.322 --> 00:52:46.273
Today's memories are in. We've
got a lot to work with here.


00:52:46.298 --> 00:52:50.437
Riley dumped her best friend, had a
miserable day at school and quit hockey.


00:52:50.462 --> 00:52:53.001
The writers had put
together a killer script.


00:52:53.032 --> 00:52:57.424
Just because Joy and Sadness are
gone, I have the stupid dream duty.


00:52:58.237 --> 00:53:00.142
Okay. How are we going to wake her up?


00:53:00.173 --> 00:53:03.155
Well. She wakes up sometimes
when she has a scary dream.


00:53:03.180 --> 00:53:04.899
- We could scare her.
- Scare her?


00:53:04.924 --> 00:53:07.253
- No no. She's been though enough already.
- But, Joy.


00:53:07.278 --> 00:53:08.776
Sadness, you may know
your way around down here.


00:53:08.801 --> 00:53:10.211
But I know Riley.


00:53:10.236 --> 00:53:13.706
We're gonna make her so happy,
she'll wake up with exhilaration


00:53:13.731 --> 00:53:17.344
- We'll excite her awake.
- That's never happen before.


00:53:17.369 --> 00:53:19.140
Woo, Riley loves dogs. Put this on.


00:53:19.165 --> 00:53:20.261
I don't think that will work.


00:53:20.286 --> 00:53:21.807
- Bing Bong.
- Yeah.


00:53:21.852 --> 00:53:25.716
- Don't let anything happen to these.
- Got it.


00:53:25.740 --> 00:53:29.349
Uh-huh. Add the reality
distortion filter.


00:53:30.456 --> 00:53:33.143
Love it. Remember, play
to the camera everyone.


00:53:33.168 --> 00:53:35.492
Riley is the camera. Make
them get out of there.


00:53:35.517 --> 00:53:39.452
We are on in 543...


00:53:40.493 --> 00:53:45.891
Hello class. Before we
begin today's pop quiz...


00:53:45.916 --> 00:53:48.840
And she is one bad actress


00:53:50.444 --> 00:53:53.842
I want to introduce our new student.


00:53:53.867 --> 00:53:56.972
Riley. Would you like
to stand up and introduce


00:53:57.159 --> 00:53:59.428
- Camera.
- Yourself.


00:53:59.789 --> 00:54:01.861
And, to Riley.


00:54:01.886 --> 00:54:03.455
My name is Riley Anderson.


00:54:03.480 --> 00:54:06.987
I'm from Minnesota and now I live here.


00:54:07.012 --> 00:54:09.832
Ew. Look, her teeth are falling out.


00:54:10.764 --> 00:54:11.810
Ew, gross.


00:54:11.835 --> 00:54:15.323
Teeth falling out. Yeah,
I'm used to that one.


00:54:16.002 --> 00:54:17.574
Let me guess. We've no pants on.


00:54:17.599 --> 00:54:19.843
Hey, look. She came to
school with no pants on.


00:54:19.868 --> 00:54:21.432
Called it!


00:54:21.457 --> 00:54:24.130
- Ready?
- I don't think this happy thing is going to work.


00:54:24.155 --> 00:54:26.409
- But if we scare her.
- Just follow my lead.


00:54:26.434 --> 00:54:27.829
Here we go.


00:54:27.854 --> 00:54:30.788
Aruu.
Bark-bark-bark.


00:54:30.813 --> 00:54:34.175
- Who is that?
- What's going on?


00:54:39.377 --> 00:54:41.770
Psst, you're on. Go.


00:54:41.795 --> 00:54:45.388
Woo. Let's party. Let's dance. Woo.


00:54:45.413 --> 00:54:47.554
Hey. A party.


00:54:48.042 --> 00:54:49.131
Bark-bark-bark.


00:54:49.156 --> 00:54:52.199
Joy, this is not working.


00:54:52.983 --> 00:54:54.409
No.


00:54:57.190 --> 00:54:57.996
Huh.


00:54:58.021 --> 00:55:00.781
Huh. Sadness, what are
you doing? Come back here.


00:55:02.089 --> 00:55:05.143
It's just a dream. It's just
a dream. It's just a dream.


00:55:06.048 --> 00:55:09.473
They're trying to wake
her up. Call security.


00:55:09.821 --> 00:55:13.087
- Hi Riley, it's me.
- Bing Bong?


00:55:17.613 --> 00:55:19.334
Sadness. You are ruining this dream.


00:55:19.359 --> 00:55:21.844
- You're scaring her.
- But look. It's working.


00:55:22.362 --> 00:55:23.256
Whoa.


00:55:23.281 --> 00:55:25.829
They're not part of
this dream. Get them.


00:55:25.854 --> 00:55:27.721
Stop right there!


00:55:28.949 --> 00:55:31.006
Pan away. Pan away.


00:55:34.244 --> 00:55:36.703
Boo. Peek and Poke line.


00:55:36.728 --> 00:55:38.433
Aw, careful.


00:55:38.458 --> 00:55:42.820
You can't do this. I know
people in Headquarters.


00:55:51.012 --> 00:55:53.775
No-no-no...


00:55:53.851 --> 00:55:56.140
There go the core memories.


00:55:58.904 --> 00:56:00.374
Come on.


00:56:01.780 --> 00:56:04.222
- What is this place?
- The subconscious.


00:56:04.254 --> 00:56:07.420
That's where they take
all the troublemakers.


00:56:11.494 --> 00:56:12.826
My hat feels loose.


00:56:12.851 --> 00:56:14.663
How do we get in?


00:56:16.060 --> 00:56:18.310
- Is that your hat?
- Yeah, it's my hat.


00:56:18.335 --> 00:56:20.342
You sure, I don't
know. Look at the label.


00:56:20.367 --> 00:56:21.440
Yeah, it says my hat.


00:56:22.465 --> 00:56:24.553
- Wait. It says my hat?
- My hat, it says.


00:56:24.578 --> 00:56:26.268
- That's what I wrote in my hat.
- What are you talking about?


00:56:26.293 --> 00:56:29.043
- Look. You got my hat on.
- Okay, it's my hat.


00:56:29.102 --> 00:56:31.964
- Hey you.
- Oh, you caught us.


00:56:32.364 --> 00:56:35.526
Get back in there. No escaping.


00:56:39.212 --> 00:56:40.705
Oh.


00:56:44.307 --> 00:56:49.372
I don't like it here. It's where
they keep Riley's darkest fears.


00:56:50.962 --> 00:56:53.358
It's broccoli.


00:56:55.212 --> 00:56:57.646
The stairs to the biggest smite.


00:56:59.084 --> 00:57:02.744
Grandma's vacuum cleaner. Aw!


00:57:09.407 --> 00:57:11.633
Okay, come on.


00:57:12.577 --> 00:57:15.215
- Would you walk quieter.
- I'm trying.


00:57:15.240 --> 00:57:16.961
What is going...


00:57:18.070 --> 00:57:20.277
Candy wrappers.


00:57:30.378 --> 00:57:32.682
- Bing Bong.
- Joy?


00:57:32.707 --> 00:57:35.650
- There you are.
- Shh.


00:57:39.722 --> 00:57:42.794
Who's the person...


00:57:55.742 --> 00:57:58.638
- Do you have the core memories?
- Yeah.


00:57:58.663 --> 00:58:01.771
All he cared about was the candy.


00:58:02.214 --> 00:58:03.695
Shh.


00:58:18.459 --> 00:58:21.539
We're outta here.
Let's get to that Train.


00:58:21.564 --> 00:58:25.544
Wait. The Train is not running.
We still have to wake up Riley.


00:58:25.569 --> 00:58:27.420
But how?


00:58:30.066 --> 00:58:31.704
Oh no.


00:58:48.724 --> 00:58:53.499
Hey Sadness. Did you hear about
the party they were having.


00:58:53.524 --> 00:58:58.060
Yeah, yes Joy. Isn't it
a bir-bir-birthday party?


00:58:58.085 --> 00:59:01.334
Did you say birthday?


00:59:01.359 --> 00:59:04.426
- And there's going to be cake and presents.
- And games and balloons.


00:59:04.451 --> 00:59:06.150
A BIRTHDAY!


00:59:06.175 --> 00:59:08.496
Okay. Follow us.


00:59:09.868 --> 00:59:12.017
Nothing like a good scare
to wake you up, right?


00:59:12.042 --> 00:59:13.612
- Okay, it's my hand writing.
- No, it isn't.


00:59:13.637 --> 00:59:16.896
- It's my hat. I wrote that.
- No, this one's my hat.


00:59:35.253 --> 00:59:38.945
- Who's the birthday girl?
- Aw!


00:59:42.170 --> 00:59:44.887
- Woo-hoo. -
Come on, let's go.


00:59:50.975 --> 00:59:53.590
- Ha ha. We made it.
- Ha ha.


00:59:53.615 --> 00:59:57.730
- Guess who's on their way to Headquarters.
- We are.


01:00:04.055 --> 01:00:06.717
- What is going on?
- He did it again.


01:00:06.742 --> 01:00:09.326
We were at school. And we were
naked. And there was a dog.


01:00:09.357 --> 01:00:11.811
The back half was... It
was-It was chasing it, I mean.


01:00:11.836 --> 01:00:14.672
- There was a Bing Bong.
- You idiot. It was a dream.


01:00:14.697 --> 01:00:18.758
This is ridiculous. We can't even
get a good night sleep anymore.


01:00:18.783 --> 01:00:20.648
Time to take action.


01:00:20.771 --> 01:00:22.840
Stupid Mon and Dad.
If they hadn't move us


01:00:22.865 --> 01:00:24.671
none of this would have happen.


01:00:24.696 --> 01:00:26.479
Who's with me?


01:00:29.969 --> 01:00:32.009
Yeah. Let's do it.


01:00:43.551 --> 01:00:45.951
She took it. There's no turning back.


01:00:45.976 --> 01:00:48.557
So. How are we going to
get to Minnesota from here.


01:00:48.582 --> 01:00:51.646
Well. Why don't we go down to the
elephant lot and rent an elephant.


01:00:51.671 --> 01:00:53.035
Hey, that sounds nice.


01:00:53.060 --> 01:00:55.713
We're taking the bus, nitwit!


01:00:56.696 --> 01:00:58.715
There is a bus leaving
tomorrow, perfect.


01:00:58.740 --> 01:01:01.159
A ticket cost money.
How do we get money?


01:01:01.184 --> 01:01:03.169
- Mom's purse.
- Oh. You wouldn't.


01:01:03.194 --> 01:01:06.922
Oh, but I would. Where
was it we saw it last?


01:01:08.476 --> 01:01:09.865
- No!
- Aw!


01:01:09.890 --> 01:01:11.342
It's downstairs somewhere.


01:01:11.367 --> 01:01:15.273
Mom and Dad got us into this
mess. They can pay to get us out.


01:01:17.626 --> 01:01:19.618
How about this... Isn't this nice?


01:01:19.643 --> 01:01:21.625
You can see everything from up here.


01:01:21.650 --> 01:01:25.054
Look. There's Inductive
Reasoning. There's Deja Vu.


01:01:25.079 --> 01:01:27.851
There's Language
Processing. There's Deja Vu.


01:01:27.876 --> 01:01:30.764
There's Critical
Thinking. There's Deja Vu.


01:01:30.789 --> 01:01:33.040
And look at this guy's memories.


01:01:33.796 --> 01:01:36.207
Hey. That was a good idea.


01:01:36.232 --> 01:01:38.440
About scaring Riley awake.


01:01:38.465 --> 01:01:41.775
- You're not so bad.
- Really?


01:01:41.800 --> 01:01:43.362
Nice work.


01:01:44.288 --> 01:01:46.289
I can't wait to get the old Riley back.


01:01:46.314 --> 01:01:49.279
As soon as we get there, I'm
going to fix this whole mess.


01:01:49.304 --> 01:01:51.053
Whoa. Is this Riley?


01:01:51.078 --> 01:01:53.472
She's so big now. She
won't fit in my rocket.


01:01:53.497 --> 01:01:54.914
How're we gonna get to the moon.


01:01:54.939 --> 01:01:57.859
Oh. It's that time in the
Twistee Treat, remember?


01:01:57.884 --> 01:02:01.960
The hockey team showed up and
Mon and Dad were there cheering.


01:02:01.985 --> 01:02:05.250
Look at her. Having fun and laughing.


01:02:05.498 --> 01:02:09.306
- I love this one.
- I love that one too.


01:02:09.331 --> 01:02:12.197
- Atta girl. Now you're getting it.
- Yeah.


01:02:12.222 --> 01:02:15.684
It was the day the Prairie
